        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>How much does a Horizon treadmill cost?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              From $699 to $1,999 on Horizon’s US store on 23 November 2026: T101 $699 (sold out), T202 $899, 7.0 AT $1,099, 7.4 AT $1,799 and 7.8 AT $1,999. Amazon had the T202 at $799.99, the 7.0 AT at $934.98 and the 7.4 AT at $1,499.99 the same day.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How much is the Horizon 7.0 AT treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              $1,099 on Horizon’s store and $934.98 on Amazon on 23 November 2026. Horizon shows a $2,100 reference price, but we have never seen it sell at that; on 14 October it was $934 with a code. Around $935 is a good price.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How much is a Horizon T101 treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Horizon lists it at $699 against a $999 reference price, but it was sold out on Horizon’s store on 23 November 2026, as it was on 14 October. Amazon had the T101 Connect at $779.67 the same day.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is Horizon cheaper on Amazon?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              On 23 November 2026, yes for three models: Amazon was $99 under Horizon on the T202, $164 under on the 7.0 AT and $299 under on the 7.4 AT. Horizon’s store codes sometimes close the gap, so check both and compare delivered prices.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Does a Horizon treadmill need a subscription?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              No. Horizon treadmills connect over Bluetooth to third-party apps such as Zwift, Kinomap and the Peloton App, and none needs a paid Horizon membership. That keeps the five-year cost close to the purchase price.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is a Horizon treadmill worth the money?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              At its usual selling prices, yes for most home walkers and joggers. The 7.0 AT, with a 20 by 60-inch deck, 15% incline, a 325 lb rating and a lifetime frame and motor warranty, has sold for under $1,000. Do not judge value against Horizon’s reference prices, which it does not charge.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

        <!-- Why trust us -->
        <section id="why-trust-us" class="ed-trust not-prose">
          <h2>Why trust Treadmill Reviews USA?</h2>
          <p>
            Every recommendation is checked against the numbers that matter for a treadmill: the maker's own
            listing and manual, at least one independent source, the warranty terms and the CPSC recall
            database. Where sources disagree we say so rather than pick a number, we say plainly when a
            machine has not been tested hands-on, and we never accept payment for a placement. <a href="/editorial-standards/">Read our review process.</a>
          </p>
